@startuml
title Signing oracle attack: forging Alice's signature
autonumber

participant "Mallory\n(registered user)" as M
participant "Server" as S
participant "Alice\n(victim oracle)" as A
participant "Bob\n(target)" as B

== Preparation ==
M -> S : GET /keys/alice, GET /keys/bob
S --> M : public keys
M -> M : choose forged message\nC = encrypt(bob key, {"from":"alice","text":"..."})\ntimestamp = now (ms)\nh = H(pad("alice", 32) || timestamp || C)

== Trigger: use Alice's client as a decryption oracle ==
M -> S : POST /messages\n{from: "mallory", to: "alice", timestamp, ciphertext: h, signature: sig_M}
S --> M : 200
S ->> A : push frame
S ->> B : push frame
B -> B : to != bob, drop

A -> A : to == alice
A -> A : verify sig_M against Mallory's key: valid
A -> A : x = decrypt(alice private key, h)\n(it's RSA, so Alice decrypting \n gives the same result as Alice signing)
A -> A : parse x as JSON: fails \n(because it's a hash, not a JSON payload)

== Bounce: Alice's client leaks the result ==
A -> S : POST /messages\n{from: "alice", to: "mallory",\nciphertext: encrypt(mallory key, {"from":"alice","text":"error: malformed message, content=hex(x)"}),\nsignature}
S ->> M : push frame
M -> M : decrypt, read hex(x)\ns = x\nnow s is a valid Alice's signature on C

== Forgery ==
M -> S : POST /messages\n{from: "alice", to: "bob", timestamp, ciphertext: C, signature: s}
S ->> B : push frame
B -> B : verify(alice key, s over H(pad(from, 32) || timestamp || C)): valid
B -> B : decrypt C, parse OK, inner from == "alice"
B -> B : display Mallory's message as from Alice

note over M, B
  With no time window there is no deadline, and s stays valid forever.
end note
@enduml
